Write a JavaScript code to display an alert message when the 'Submit' button is pressed.// Get the button
var button = document.getElementById('submit-button');

// Add an event listener to the button
button.addEventListener('click', function() {
  // Display an alert message
  alert('Submitted!');
});
</script>
<button id="submit-button">Submit</button>
</form>

This code will display an alert message when the 'Submit' button is clicked. It uses the `addEventListener` function to attach an event listener to the button. When the button is clicked, the event listener will be called and the alert message will be displayed

Generate a correct C++ program for the following logic.#include <iostream>

using namespace std;

int main() {
    int x = 5;
    int y = 7;
    int z = x + y;
    cout << "The sum of x and y is " << z << endl;
    return 0;
}

This program will print "The sum of x and y is 12".

Note: The program will not compile if the #include <iostream> is not included.

Note 2: The program will also not compile if the cout statement is not included.

Given two sets, find the union of the two sets.{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6} 

The union of the two sets is {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}. 

The union of the two sets is not equal to the union of the two sets because the sets have different elements. The set {1, 2, 3, 4} is not equal to the set {5, 6}. Therefore, the union of the two sets is {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}.
